ntent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-04T15:46:58Z","updated_at":"2025-08-04T15:49:41Z","body":"The reason it crashes after dev4 is because your CPU is too old to support Godot 4.5, it doesn't support SSE 4.2 which is required (you are using a CPU that's 17 years old)\n\nAs a workaround you can run the x86_32 version of the editor which doesn't require SSE 4.2\n\nSo this could be related to that in 4.4.1 as well, Godot can't really be expected to work on such old hardware","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3151302540/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3151613704","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109279#issuecomment-3151613704","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109279","id":3151613704,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc672c8I","user":{"login":"knightmb","id":3860711,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NjA3MTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3860711?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/knightmb","html_url":"https://github.com/knightmb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knightmb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knightmb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knightmb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knightmb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knightmb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knightmb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knightmb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knightmb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knightmb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-04T17:05:15Z","updated_at":"2025-08-04T17:05:15Z","body":"While the crashing issue is related to SSE4.2 (which I will update in a separate bug I've created), it wouldn't explain why it works in Windows 10 on the same system, but on Linux, on the same identical hardware; it does not?\n\nThis might be moot though, I tested it on this system:\n**Godot v4.4.1.stable - Mageia 8 on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GT 1030 (nvidia) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-2400 CPU @ 3.10GHz (4 threads)**\n\nThe mentioned above system works properly with the same v4.4.1.stable.official - Linux\n\nSo, the difference in processor generation appears to be the sticking point in some aspects, just not on the same hardware with only the OS changing? It's odd though, everything else on this processor generation works fine without any issues (v4.4.1.stable) on both Linux and Windows, the only issue encountered is just a minor issue that is easy to get around. I wonder what makes the Streaming SIMD Extensions 4.2 so vital to this? But it's not really the scope of this bug report.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3151613704/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3151636739","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109279#issuecomment-3151636739","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109279","id":3151636739,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc672ikD","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-04T17:09:00Z","updated_at":"2025-08-04T17:09:00Z","body":"There's no bug related to SSE 4.2, your device doesn't support it so it's not a bug, so please do not open a report for that\n\nBut that just highlights that this is likely a processor issue as it does work with a more modern CPU","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3151636739/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3151738055","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109279#issuecomment-3151738055","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109279","id":3151738055,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6727TH","user":{"login":"knightmb","id":3860711,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4NjA3MTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3860711?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/knightmb","html_url":"https://github.com/knightmb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knightmb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knightmb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knightmb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knightmb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knightmb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knightmb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knightmb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knightmb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/knightmb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-04T17:25:26Z","updated_at":"2025-08-04T17:25:26Z","body":"I agree about the SSE4.2, but to get back on topic. Simply swapping operating systems on the same hardware should produce the same results in both Linux and Windows, in theory. Currently, it only happens in Linux and **not** Windows on the same hardware. That is my only point.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3151738055/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray"